    "section_evoo_v3_faq_rRJhLR": {
      "type": "section-evoo-v3-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_item_wg78Aq": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I take AIWO Prebiotik-D with probiotic supplements?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes — prebiotics and probiotics are complementary. Prebiotics feed beneficial bacteria; probiotics introduce them. Used together (a synbiotic approach),you are both adding beneficial strains and ensuring they have the substrate to survive and multiply. Bifidobacterium specifically thrives on inulin-type fructans — making AIWO Prebiotik-D an ideal companion to any Bifidobacterium probiotic supplement.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_BFc6Am": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is the difference between prebiotics and probiotics?",
            "answer": "<p> Probiotics are live bacteria added from outside — supplements or fermented foods. Prebiotics are the fibres that feed the bacteria already living in your gut.<br/>Most people focus on adding bacteria without first ensuring the environment can<br/>support them. AIWO Prebiotik-D feeds your existing microbiome particularly<br/>Bifidobacterium and Lactobacillus the strains most associated with gut health,immunity, and mood regulation.<br/><br/></p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_pgG9dR": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Why does AIWO Prebiotik-D use both oligofructose and inulin?",
            "answer": "<p>The two fibres ferment at different rates and in different gut zones. Oligofructose has a shorter chain length it is fermented earlier, in the proximal colon and small intestine, providing a rapid bifidogenic effect. Inulin has a longer chain it travels further into the large intestine, providing sustained fermentation and deeper microbiome support. Together, they cover the full length of the gut rather than a single section.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_zet6LP": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Who benefits most from AIWO Prebiotik-D?",
            "answer": "<p>Adults looking to support their gut microbiome diversity, immune health,<br/>and digestive regularity. Particularly relevant for those with low-fibre diets, high antibiotic use history, urban lifestyles with processed food exposure, or anyone seeking to support the gut-brain axis as part of a longevity protocol. Consult your physician before use if pregnant, nursing, or on medication.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_Q6TUxh": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is AIWO Prebiotik-D vegan?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. AIWO Prebiotik-D is certified vegan, GMO-free, and pesticide-free. It contains no animal-derived ingredients. The active ingredient is derived from chicory root via Beneo Orafti a globally recognised plant-sourced prebiotic ingredient supplier. It also carries Kosher certification (U symbol).</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_WyBt4K": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How should I start taking it?",
            "answer": "<p>Start with one 4g scoop mixed in hot water daily. If tolerated well, you can gradually increase to a maximum of 15g per day. Starting low and increasing slowly allows your microbiome to adapt without discomfort (gas or bloating can occur with rapid dose increases in those unaccustomed to prebiotic fibre). Keep tightly closed after every use. Store in a cool, dry place.<br/></p>"
          }
        }
